WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
One demonstration. Autonomous press-and-turn cap removal.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:12.500
The demo provides intent, stage order, and key contact relations—not a trajectory to replay.

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:19.500
Agent plans arrival; relative pose defines interaction; touch decides when to switch.

4
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Aligned RGB-D establishes a robot_aligned cap task frame in the FR3 base frame.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Grounding sets the target; planning sets the path; touch gates the transition into twisting.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Task geometry sets the angle; touch supervises contact; wrist travel triggers automatic regrasp.

7
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Release becomes eligible only after one turn; first record the upfeed resistance peak.

8
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.200
0.077 and 0.115 stay below 35% of peak, creating a thread-release candidate.

9
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.000
A stationary window remains low at 0.057 while contact remains: thread release, not contact loss.

10
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Run 16 ends at LIFT_CAP: 540 degrees, five regrasps, release_verified, and a 30 mm lift.
